# Data

- One adapter per vendor. Register in the provider registry. Business modules never import a vendor module directly except through the registry.
- Every fetch returns a QualityEnvelope: source, timestamp, retrieved_at, confidence, data_quality, errors.
- Quality checks: null, duplicate, stale, outlier, timestamp error, API error, schema mismatch.
- Rate-limit, timeout, and 4xx/5xx must be mapped to structured SourceStatus, not raised through the UI as a crash.
- Missing API keys produce `missing_key` status and empty payload — not placeholder coins or matches.
- Providers are replaceable. Interface first, vendor second.
